"""Local bilingual editorial revision; preserve evidence identifiers and provenance."""
from pathlib import Path
import re,json
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
edits={'zh':[
('员工用 AI 做成一项工作之后', '一项 AI 方法能否成为团队可以依靠的工作资源，需要在交接之后判断。本文从共享新闻跟踪实践出发，结合知识转移与组织惯例研究，区分方法执行、适用范围判断和修订回传三个环节。接收者能够生成结果，未必意味着结果适合其岗位；个人完成了修改，也未必意味着下一位同事能够获得更新。本文据此提出，以延后使用的质量、异常处置和全部参与者的投入评价复用，考察交接支持、岗位差异及维护安排的作用，并设计公开材料分析与受控行为比较相衔接的研究路线。个人经验的组织价值，应体现在同事能否持续完成工作，以及维持这种能力需要付出多少劳动。'),
('春节期间，一个研究团队', '2026 年春节，腾讯研究院 AI 原生小组共享了一项跟踪 AI 动态的 Skill。成员每天调用，依据结果继续修改；假期结束后，这项工具仍被用于日常跟踪。[S09] 值得关注的是，一次假期任务留下的方法进入了后续工作。'),
('CAPTION1：', 'CAPTION1：新闻跟踪方法的持续使用。图示概括报告记载的共享、调用、迭代和节后使用过程。持续使用不等于已经证明净收益；报告未提供质量对照、维护工时或完整使用日志。[S09]'),
('这个故事的吸引力', '这类延续使一次任务中的投入有机会服务后来的工作。报告还以新成员加入团队的假设情境，说明同事如何交出可运行的 Skill，接收者如何使用、修改，再将改动送回。[S09] 从交出方法到接回修订，经验不再只由最初的制作者掌握。'),
('这项实践已经是团队共享活动', '这一案例呈现的是共同使用，尚未追踪方法最初由谁提出、怎样从个人尝试转为集体采用。它留下的问题是：员工在自己的工作中摸索出的 AI 方法，怎样才能让同事接得住，并在后续任务中继续用下去？'),
('把个人经验做成工具', '报告中的安克案例提供了另一种起点：一名非程序员用三个月搭建供应链运营系统，另一名员工用两个月搭建亚马逊 Case 自动提交、监控和回复系统。安克另设“火箭班”，让获选员工集中解决真实业务问题，再回到原团队。这些记录展示了个人制作工具及组织推动经验回流的尝试，但未追踪同事后续使用，也未说明上述制作者是否参加火箭班。[S09]'),
('这几处记录共同指出', '做出工具、交给同事和持续复用，需要不同的证据。制作者完成任务，说明方法在原场景中可能有用；同事借助它完成自己的工作，才提供了直接的复用证据；条件变化后能否继续使用，还需追踪。如果把这些过程一并算作“推广成功”，工具数量、演示和培训容易遮住反复求助、重新配置与最终放弃。本文将交接及其后续使用作为观察单位，讨论个人方法何时能够支持团队的共同工作。'),
('一个人做出的 AI 简报', '一份 AI 简报通常带着制作者的工作习惯：哪些来源值得追踪，哪些消息上周已经讨论过，某个含糊的名称指的是哪项产品。提示词传给同事时，这些判断未必随之传递。接收者可能没有原文件的访问权限，也可能面向另一类读者，需要产品何时上线，而非模型能力如何变化。同一份提示词虽然成功运行，结果仍可能用不到当天的工作中。'),
('本文将团队可复用能力界定为', '本文把团队可复用能力界定为：原制作者之外的成员能够在既定任务范围内持续完成工作，并恰当地处理超出范围或无法完成的情况。方法及其材料是可共享的资源；成员后续的表现才体现团队是否具备相应能力。评价因此涵盖延后使用的质量、异常处置和所有参与者的投入，而交接说明、适配帮助与维护安排是可能解释这些结果的条件。求助并不意味着复用失败，但若每次运行都要制作者陪同，就应把这部分劳动计入，而不能仅凭一次点击认定交接已经完成。'),
('研究因而需要区分三个事件', '观察需要区分制作者完成原任务、接收者首次完成自己的任务，以及接收者在后续任务中再次使用。它们不构成固定的成长阶段：方法可能由多人共同制作，接收者也可能先修改再运行。一次双人交接可以揭示困难及其解决过程，却只是团队能力的局部证据；判断稳定复用，还需覆盖不同成员、相关任务和不同时间。'),
('生成式 AI 使这一老问题', '生成式 AI 为这一既有问题增加了新的研究条件。自然语言既能向同事解释方法，也能指挥系统执行；接收者可能在尚未充分理解方法时，就得到看似可用的结果。但复制指令并不会自动复制模型、连接工具与上下文。这与封装改变组织活动可见性的理论讨论有关。[S03] 当部分执行交给系统，谁决定任务目的、界定适用范围并负责更新，也需要重新考察。[S04] 关键在于：同事能否运行，能否判断何时适用，以及有用的修订能否到达后续使用者。'),
('例如，同事已经能用共享方法', '例如，同事能用共享方法生成简报后，制作者可能认为交接已经结束。接收者却开始面向另一岗位发送简报，改变关注范围，并反复请求补充信息。文件看似相同，承担的工作却已变化。能够运行降低了尝试门槛，并不足以保证适合新用途。传统自动化同样面临这一问题；生成式 AI 值得进一步研究之处，在于以日常语言制作和修改的方法如何被不同岗位的人理解、采用和调整。'),
('沿用新闻跟踪任务', '以每日 AI 简报为例，一份可交接的方法应先让同事弄清楚：为谁整理、关注什么，以及哪些问题不在处理范围内。随后列出可用来源、所需材料和访问条件，让接收者能开始工作，而不是等运行失败后再逐项猜测。图 2 是据此提出的方法页示意，并非报告中的原始 Skill。'),
('把这些条件带到交接现场', '交接材料应与任务相称。一次性的简单任务，提示词加一个示例可能足够；每周重复、多人参与且依赖共享数据的任务，则可能需要明确的操作条件与维护安排，否则每次使用都要重新摸索。任务频率也不是唯一依据。能力形成理论提示，低频任务难以通过反复实践积累经验，也可能从知识编码中受益。[A04] 判断交接是否充分，应结合任务差异、重复性及持续时间，不能以文档长短代替。'),
('同样，默会经验不会', '方法页也无法容纳全部默会经验。有些问题要到同事处理自己的任务时才会显现：简报运行正常，选出的新闻却对另一个业务团队没有用。这可能是关注范围不同，并非执行故障。让接收者先试用，再讨论具体调整，能把原先没有说清的判断带入交接。制作者解释来源选择，接收者说明新用途需要的信息，双方才有机会形成适合后续工作的版本。这一过程与将知识转移视为持续活动的研究相呼应。[A03]'),
('一个需要检验的问题由此产生', '由此可以检验一种可能的脱节：条件变化后，方法仍能生成结果，接收者却没有重新判断它是否适用；接收者即便完成了修改，同事拿到的也可能仍是旧版。运行、判断和回传需要分别记录。反过来，如果三者无需额外支持也能协调维持，或者执行情况已足以解释后续表现，进一步区分它们的解释价值就会受到限制。'),
('工具交到第二个人手里以后', '交接之后，同事会带来新的需求：有人调整关注主题，有人需要原始来源，也有人发现链接已经失效。这些问题可以逐个交回制作者，也可以更新共享材料，或保留服务于不同岗位的版本。每一种选择都涉及时间。团队需要判断哪些修改值得共同维护，并为承担这项工作的人留出时间。'),
('报告中“改完再扔回去”', '报告所描述的修订回传提示了接收者参与改进的可能，但回传之后仍需取舍。销售团队偏好的摘要长度，未必适合研发团队；增加来源可以扩充信息，也可能延长另一岗位的筛选时间。把所有修改合并到一版，可能消除重复劳动，也可能破坏原有用途。共享版本可以保留稳定部分，通过明确选项或独立变体处理岗位差异。版本应怎样划分，取决于任务的相似程度与维护成本。'),
('这与组织惯例研究', '组织惯例研究关注共同模式与实际执行的关系：共享方法约束工作，也在使用中被重新解释。因此，文档一致并不足以说明团队形成了共同能力，还需观察成员怎样运用方法，以及修改怎样进入下一次执行。[S01] 对生成式工具，变化可能发生在提示词、输入材料、模型选择或外部连接中；仅统计提示词版本会遗漏这些差别。'),
('维护还涉及时间与贡献归属', '维护劳动往往不如首次演示醒目。制作工具的人可能得到认可，之后解释限制、回答问题、更新依赖的人却未必获得同等关注。支持需求如果持续叠加在制作者的本职工作上，工具越受欢迎，个人负担反而可能越重。接收者也可能只修好自己的副本，来不及把改动送回。复用究竟节省了劳动，还是将劳动集中到少数人、分散到互不相通的副本，需要实际记录才能判断。'),
('因此，一次分享获得多少赞', '比分享获得多少赞更有用的信息，是同事第一次运行前做了什么准备，遇到变化时向谁求助，以及一次修复能否减少后来者的重复劳动。组织可以为适配和支持安排时间，记录修订贡献，并明确问题由谁接收。共同维护也有成本：一个频繁变化、很少再用的工具，未必值得长期保留统一版本。'),
('腾讯报告将组织变化的一部分动力', '共享 Skill 的实践把组织变革落在了一项普通任务上：员工共同使用、持续修改，方法得以留在日常工作中。[S09] 对管理者而言，这意味着评价不能止于工具是否做出来，还要追踪同事接手后的表现，以及维护是否有人承担。'),
('这不要求每位员工都成为开发者', '团队的共同积累可以来自不同贡献。有人识别重复任务，有人把方法做成工具，有人提供判断质量所需的样例，也有人持续更新和答疑。承认这些劳动，才能让奖励与实际协作相对应。投入交接与维护是否值得，应由任务结果和总体投入判断，而非使用 AI 的时长。'),
('这种做法也有边界', '并非每种方法都值得推广。很少重复的任务可能直接完成更合适；岗位目标差异较大时，借鉴思路可能比复制工具更有用；涉及特殊权限或专业责任的工作，则需要限定接收者与使用范围。清楚说明何时不应使用，也是共同方法的一部分。'),
('个人 AI 经验成为团队能力', '个人 AI 经验的价值，最终要在同事的工作中得到检验：接手者能否完成任务，过一段时间能否继续使用，以及谁承担了让方法保持可用的劳动。以这些问题追踪交接，既能保留员工自主探索的空间，也能识别哪些经验值得沉淀、怎样维护，以及何时应当停止复用。')],
'en':[
('After an employee uses AI', "An AI method becomes a resource that a team can rely on only if colleagues can use it beyond the original task. Drawing on shared news-tracking practice, knowledge transfer and organizational routines, this Perspective distinguishes execution, judgments of applicability and the return of revisions. A recipient may generate an output without recognizing that it does not fit a new role; a useful local change may never reach the next user. Reuse should therefore be assessed through delayed task quality, responses to exceptions and effort across participants. The proposed research links analysis of public materials with controlled behavioral comparisons to examine handover support, differences between roles and maintenance arrangements. The organizational value of personal know-how lies in colleagues' continued ability to complete work, considered alongside the labor needed to sustain it."),
('During the Spring Festival holiday', "During the 2026 Spring Festival holiday, Tencent Research Institute's AI-native group shared a Skill for tracking AI developments. Members used it daily and revised it in response to the output. The tool remained in everyday use after the holiday.[S09] A method developed around a temporary task had become part of subsequent work."),
('CAPTION1:', 'CAPTION1: Continued use of a news-tracking method. The figure summarizes the reported sequence of sharing, use, revision and continued use after the holiday. Continued use does not establish a net benefit: the report provides no comparative quality assessment, maintenance hours or complete usage logs.[S09]'),
('What makes this account interesting', 'Such continuity allows effort invested in one task to serve later work. The report also uses a hypothetical newcomer scenario to describe a colleague handing over a runnable Skill, the recipient using and modifying it, and the changes being returned.[S09] Receiving revisions as well as sharing a method gives recipients a part in its further development.'),
('The reported practice was already', 'The case describes collective use, without tracing who first proposed the method or how individual experimentation became collective adoption. It leaves a practical question: how can employees hand over the AI methods they develop so that colleagues can use them in their own work and keep doing so?'),
('Page 17 of the same report', "The report's Anker cases offer a different starting point. One employee without a programming background built a supply-chain operations system in three months; another built a system for automatically submitting, monitoring and responding to Amazon Cases in two months. A separate initiative, Rocket Class, gave selected employees time to solve real business problems before returning to their original teams. These accounts describe tool creation and efforts to bring experience back into teams. They do not track colleagues' subsequent use or establish whether the system builders participated in Rocket Class.[S09]"),
('Together, these accounts identify', "Building, handing over and sustaining use require different evidence. Completion by the maker suggests that a method may be useful in its original setting. A colleague completing their own task with it provides direct evidence of reuse; continued use under changed conditions requires follow-up. Treating all three as successful adoption allows tool counts, demonstrations and training attendance to obscure repeated help-seeking, reconfiguration and abandonment. This Perspective takes the handover and subsequent use as its unit of observation, asking when personal methods can support shared work."),
('An AI briefing may suit', "An AI briefing carries its maker's working habits: which sources deserve attention, which stories were discussed last week, and which product an ambiguous name denotes. Passing on a prompt need not pass on these judgments. A recipient may lack access to the original files or serve readers who need to know when a product launches, rather than how model capabilities have changed. The same prompt can run successfully while producing little that the recipient can use that day."),
("We define a team's capability", "A team's capability for reuse is defined here as members other than the original maker being able to complete work repeatedly within a specified task domain and respond appropriately to out-of-scope or uncompleted tasks. Methods and materials are shareable resources; subsequent performance indicates whether the team has the corresponding capability. Outcomes therefore include delayed task quality, responses to exceptions and effort across participants. Instructions, adaptation assistance and maintenance arrangements may explain these outcomes. Seeking help is compatible with reuse, but if every run requires the maker's presence, that labor must be counted. One successful click does not establish a completed handover."),
('Research should consequently distinguish', 'Observation needs to distinguish the maker completing the original task, a recipient first completing their own task, and that recipient using the method again. These are not fixed developmental stages: methods may be jointly developed, and recipients may modify them before first use. A two-person handover can reveal difficulties and how they are resolved, but offers only partial evidence of team capability. Stable reuse requires observations across members, relevant tasks and time.'),
('Generative AI brings together', 'Generative AI introduces distinctive conditions into this established problem. Natural language can explain a method to colleagues and instruct a system to execute it, allowing recipients to obtain apparently usable results before understanding the method fully. Yet copying instructions does not reproduce the model, connected tools or context. This relates to theoretical accounts of how encapsulation changes the visibility of organizational activities.[S03] When execution passes partly to a system, responsibility for setting purposes, judging scope and arranging updates also warrants examination.[S04] The questions are whether a colleague can run the method, judge when it applies, and return useful revisions to subsequent users.'),
('For example, a colleague may already', 'Once a colleague can generate a briefing, its maker may regard the handover as complete. The recipient may nevertheless begin circulating it to a different role, change its focus and repeatedly request additional information. The file appears unchanged, but the work it serves has shifted. Being able to run a method lowers the threshold for trying it without ensuring fitness for a new purpose. Conventional automation faces this difficulty too. Generative AI offers an opportunity to examine how people in different roles understand, adopt and adapt methods created and modified in everyday language.'),
('The news-tracking task makes', 'For a daily AI brief, a usable handover should first establish whom it serves, what it covers and which questions fall outside its scope. Available sources, required materials and access conditions should follow, allowing the recipient to start work without discovering each missing requirement through a failed run. Figure 2 illustrates a method sheet built around these needs; it is not the original Skill from the report.'),
('Bringing these conditions into', 'Handover materials should fit the task. A prompt and an example may suffice for a simple, one-off activity. Weekly work involving several people and shared data may need explicit operating conditions and maintenance arrangements; without them, each use can become a fresh attempt to work out the method. Frequency is not the only consideration. Theory on capability development suggests that codification may also benefit infrequent tasks, for which experience is difficult to accumulate through repetition.[A04] Adequacy should be judged against task differences, repetition and duration, rather than documentation length.'),
('Nor does a method sheet', "A method sheet cannot capture all tacit experience. Some questions emerge when colleagues encounter their own tasks: a briefing runs correctly, but its news is of little use to another business team. The problem may be scope rather than execution. Trying the method and discussing specific adjustments can bring previously unstated judgments into the handover. As makers explain source choices and recipients specify what a new use requires, they may develop a version suited to subsequent work. This process accords with research treating knowledge transfer as a continuing activity.[A03]"),
('This raises a question for investigation', 'One possible disconnect can therefore be tested: after conditions change, the method still produces output, but the recipient does not reconsider its applicability. Even a successful local revision may leave colleagues using an older version. Execution, judgment and the return of revisions need separate records. Conversely, if these activities remain coordinated without extra support, or execution alone explains subsequent performance adequately, the value of distinguishing them would be limited.'),
('Further work becomes visible', 'After the handover, colleagues bring new requirements: one changes the topic, another needs original sources, and a third finds a broken link. Each problem might return to the maker, prompt a shared update or lead to a version for a particular role. Every option takes time. Teams need to decide which changes warrant collective maintenance and allocate time to those doing the work.'),
("The report's scenario of modifying", "The report's account of returning revisions suggests a role for recipients in improving the method, but returned changes still require decisions. A summary length preferred by sales may not suit research and development; adding sources may broaden coverage while extending another user's screening time. Merging all changes may remove duplicated effort while impairing existing uses. Shared versions can preserve stable components, with options or separate variants accommodating role differences. The choice depends on task similarity and maintenance costs."),
('This connects to the relationship', 'Organizational routines research examines the relationship between shared patterns and particular performances: methods constrain work while being reinterpreted in use. Consistent documents therefore do not establish shared capability; observation must also follow how members use methods and how revisions enter subsequent work.[S01] For generative tools, changes can occur in prompts, input materials, model choices or external connections. Counting prompt versions alone would miss these differences.'),
('Maintenance also raises questions', 'Maintenance is often less visible than an initial demonstration. A tool maker may receive recognition, while those explaining limitations, answering questions and updating dependencies receive less attention. If support accumulates alongside the maker\'s existing duties, popularity may increase their burden. Recipients may also repair personal copies without finding time to return changes. Whether reuse saves labor, concentrates it among a few people or disperses it across disconnected copies is an empirical question.'),
('Reactions to a shared tool', 'More useful than reactions to a shared tool are accounts of what colleagues prepare before first use, whom they approach when conditions change, and whether a repair saves later users from repeating the work. Organizations can allocate time for adaptation and support, recognize revisions and clarify who receives requests. Collective maintenance also costs time: a frequently changing, rarely reused tool may not warrant a common version.'),
("Tencent's report locates", 'The shared Skill brings organizational change into an ordinary task: employees use a method together, revise it and retain it in everyday work.[S09] For managers, evaluation should therefore extend beyond tool creation to colleagues\' subsequent performance and the allocation of maintenance work.'),
('This does not require every employee', 'A team can build shared resources through different contributions. Some employees identify recurring tasks, others turn methods into tools, others provide examples needed to judge quality, and others maintain the method and answer questions. Recognizing these contributions aligns credit with the work of collaboration. Whether handover and maintenance deserve further investment depends on task outcomes and total effort, rather than hours spent using AI.'),
('There are limits.', 'Not every method warrants wider use. Rarely repeated tasks may be better completed directly; where roles serve different purposes, borrowing an idea may be more useful than copying a tool. Work involving restricted access or professional responsibility requires limits on recipients and uses. Knowing when not to use a method is part of making it shareable.'),
('Turning personal AI know-how', "The value of personal AI know-how is ultimately tested in colleagues' work: whether recipients complete their tasks, whether they can use the method again later, and who supplies the labor that keeps it usable. Following these questions preserves room for employees' own experimentation while identifying which methods merit retention, how they should be maintained and when reuse should stop.")]
}
log=[]
for lang,items in edits.items():
 p=R/f'manuscript_{lang}.md';blocks=re.split(r'\n\s*\n',p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').strip())
 for prefix,new in items:
  found=[i for i,b in enumerate(blocks) if b.startswith(prefix)]
  assert len(found)==1,(lang,prefix,found)
  i=found[0];log.append({'language':lang,'before':blocks[i],'after':new});blocks[i]=new
 p.write_text('\n\n'.join(blocks)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
(R/'revision03_language_changes.json').write_text(json.dumps(log,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Revised',len(log),'paragraphs; source identifiers retained.')
